Terraform SNS and SQS Messaging Infrastructure
Project Overview
This task provisions a simple messaging integration using Terraform and the AWS provider. The infrastructure is deployed against the configured LocalStack-compatible AWS endpoints in the us-east-1 region.

The configuration creates:
- An Amazon SNS topic named nautilus-sns-topic.
- An Amazon SQS queue named nautilus-sqs-queue.
- An SQS queue policy that permits Amazon SNS to send messages to the queue, restricted to the configured SNS topic.
- An SNS subscription that connects the topic to the SQS queue using the sqs protocol.
Terraform also exposes the SNS topic ARN and SQS queue URL as output values.
